invariant: INV-17
file: sha512_hw.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh sha2-equiv
reason: sha512_of_hw returns without wiping the context it hashed in, so its
  dead frame keeps the end of the input and the digest's eight words. The
  digest is still right, so no vector sees it. bin/sha2_equiv_test copies
  the stack below one sha512_of_hw call and looks for two 64-bit words in
  a row that the call computed from its input. The script runs the arm64
  binary under qemu-aarch64. The lane skips without docker, and this then
  reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    sha512_final_hw(&s, out);
    ct_wipe(&s, sizeof s);
--- new
    sha512_final_hw(&s, out);
